4. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` body: `OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields` blank-check; if any missing → `MissingOwnerFieldsException` → 400.
5. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` (id/pets ignored → new entity).
6. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` opens `@Transactional`; no other side effects.
7. `ownerRepository.save(owner)` → Spring Data `persist`; Hibernate `PrePersist` re-validates entity constraints (incl. stricter `telephone` regex); id generated (IDENTITY).
8. On commit, any DB constraint violation → `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404.
9. `toOwnerDto(owner)`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.

There are no application event listeners, no JPA lifecycle callbacks in source, no custom constraint validators, no notification/audit/password logic anywhere on this path.
